{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>When they had finished.</b> Perhaps the intention is that there remained only enough for the duration of their going and returning, and Scripture says even of this ״כִּלּוּ״ (they finished) because they need to bring more. Or according to what they said, their memory for blessing (Ta'anit 10a), that Jacob had prepared grain for two years of famine, they would eat during the journey there and back from the provisions that were with him. Therefore the verse was precise in saying ״כִּלּוּ הַשֶּׁבֶר אֲשֶׁר הֵבִיאוּ מִמִּצְרַיִם״ — to say that the grain they brought from Egypt they finished, but not all the grain that they had."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:48:13.626137569Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}